WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.460 --> 00:00:04.410
- So this weekend is WrestleMania

00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:07.220
and it got me thinking about a wrestler

00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:09.310
by the name of Bret The Hit Man Hart.

00:00:09.310 --> 00:00:11.370
So you see Bret Hart was a wrestler

00:00:11.370 --> 00:00:14.710
in the WWF, now WWE, for a very long time.

00:00:14.710 --> 00:00:16.790
Originally as a tag team partner

00:00:16.790 --> 00:00:19.940
of Jim The Anvil Neidhart,
known as The Hart Foundation

00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:21.940
and he had a very nice career in the early

00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:24.810
to mid 80s through into the late 80s

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:26.680
and then into the early 90s

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:28.500
and then in the early 90s he broke out

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:31.370
as an individual star and
he's now widely considered

00:00:31.370 --> 00:00:34.690
probably one of the best 10
to 15 wrestlers of all time.

00:00:34.690 --> 00:00:37.950
Why am I talking about
Bret The Hit Man Hart

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:39.990
in a video that's probably
predicated on thoughts

00:00:39.990 --> 00:00:42.080
around business, it's because of this.

00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:46.370
Bret Hart's nickname was
The Excellence of Execution

00:00:46.370 --> 00:00:47.920
and I've been giving a
lot of thought lately

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:51.800
to where the world's at
right now and the lack

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:55.470
of people's understanding of
how much execution matters.

00:00:55.470 --> 00:00:57.790
I've realized that I'm
not investing in as many

00:00:57.790 --> 00:01:00.700
startups lately because
a lot of the people

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:04.610
have very nice ideas but
I've watched so many,

00:01:04.610 --> 00:01:09.020
so many bright, brilliant,
hungry, ambitious,

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:12.830
talented 22- to 26-year-olds

00:01:12.830 --> 00:01:15.990
in the last couple years
just completely fail

00:01:15.990 --> 00:01:18.880
because they didn't have
the gut and or experience

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:21.820
and or nuances to navigate
through the execution

00:01:21.820 --> 00:01:25.260
of what it took to build a
business or, more importantly,

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:27.230
the ability to adjust half-way through

00:01:27.230 --> 00:01:30.570
as this world moves so
quickly that they're not able

00:01:30.570 --> 00:01:32.810
to change their business
model when the world

00:01:32.810 --> 00:01:35.120
changes on them based on the prominence

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:36.340
of how they launched their company.

00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:39.240
See, I get a lot of emails
from friends on Facebook

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:41.010
like oh, my God, you're so lucky,

00:01:41.010 --> 00:01:42.380
it all happened so fast.

00:01:42.380 --> 00:01:43.700
It didn't happen fast.

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:46.210
I've been fucking
executing since I was 14.

00:01:46.210 --> 00:01:49.050
In a Malcolm Gladwell
world of 10,000 hours

00:01:49.050 --> 00:01:52.180
and you're an expert,
I put in 50,000 hours.

00:01:52.180 --> 00:01:54.470
The reason I failed every
class is 'cause I was running

00:01:54.470 --> 00:01:56.530
businesses since I was 14-years-old.

00:01:56.530 --> 00:01:58.800
Everybody's like oh Wine
Library TV is such a phenomenon.

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:03.140
I ran Wine Library, a wine
retail and ecommerce business

00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:07.200
from 1998 until early
2006 every single day

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:11.520
for 17 hours a day before
I started Wine Library TV

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:13.060
to get internet famous.

00:02:13.060 --> 00:02:16.340
See, execution matters and
putting in the work matters.

00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:18.930
Bret Hart grew up in a wrestling family.

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:22.180
He was eight and nine when
he was in The Squared Circle

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:24.500
every day getting thrown
around like a rag doll

00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:26.690
by his older brothers and his dad.

00:02:26.690 --> 00:02:29.690
Put in the work, execute,
and then you've got a shot.

00:02:29.690 --> 00:02:32.720
Your ideas are cute and
all but without execution

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:33.970
most of you will fail.

00:02:33.970 --> 00:02:36.940
It is time, in 2013, that we start getting

00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:39.420
dramatically more
practical and start looking

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:41.747
at people that are 28, 29, 42, 49,

00:02:41.747 --> 00:02:44.400
50, 57, and understand
yeah, maybe they don't know

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:48.253
what Snapchat is but their
execution value is high.

